g-name>, <string-name><surname>Bunning</surname> <given-names>ML</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Beaty</surname> <given-names>BJ</given-names></string-name> <article-title>Epitope-blocking enzyme-linked immunosorbent assays for detection of West Nile virus antibodies in domestic mammals.</article-title><source>J Clin Microbiol</source> <year>2003</year>;<volume>41</volume>:<fpage>2676</fpage>&#x02013;<lpage>9</lpage> <pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1128/JCM.41.6.2676-2679.2003</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12791902</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="R7"><label>7. </label><citation citation-type="book"><string-name><surname>Sabattini</surname> <given-names>MS</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Avil&#x000e9;s</surname> <given-names>G</given-names></string-name>, <string-name><surname>Monath</surname> <given-names>TP</given-names></string-name> Historical, epidemiological and ecological aspects of arbovirus in Argentina: Flaviviridae, Bunyaviridae and Rhabdoviridae. In: Travassos da Rosa APA, Vasconcelos PFC, Travassos da Rosa JFS, editors. An overview of arbovirology in Brazil and neighboring countries. Belem (Brazil); Instituto Evandro Chagas; <year>1998</year> p. 113&#x02013;34.</citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>